WEBVTT

00:00.980 --> 00:02.870
I'm so sorry we were late.

00:02.870 --> 00:05.010
Not at all. You must be busy.

00:05.010 --> 00:07.450
You're one of Japan's 
best detectives, after all.

00:07.450 --> 00:09.570
Who told you that?!

00:09.570 --> 00:12.360
I have a friend in the prefectural police.

00:12.360 --> 00:15.000
They asked Kawasemi-san 
about brilliant detectives,

00:15.000 --> 00:17.660
and he gave your name, Isshiki-san.

00:18.010 --> 00:19.870
K-Kawasemi-san did?

00:19.870 --> 00:24.840
But why invite a brilliant detective 
to a meteor shower viewing party?

00:25.210 --> 00:27.130
To be prepared for anything!

00:27.640 --> 00:32.360
A few of our guests will inevitably
be thinking about the incident.

00:32.360 --> 00:33.400
"The incident"?

00:33.400 --> 00:34.930
Wh-What kind of incident?

00:34.930 --> 00:36.180
Don't ask that!

00:36.630 --> 00:39.270
I'm here to get away from cases.

00:39.270 --> 00:40.900
But just asking isn't...

00:40.900 --> 00:42.200
No, I can't!

00:42.200 --> 00:44.900
What if I just happen to hear about one?

00:44.900 --> 00:47.820
Then there'd be no point to any of this!

00:44.900 --> 00:47.820
Please don't mind him. He's a little tired.

00:48.460 --> 00:51.500
I asked you to come just as insurance.

00:51.500 --> 00:53.320
Nothing's going to happen.

00:53.320 --> 00:56.030
Please enjoy the viewing party.

00:57.200 --> 01:00.260
Look, you can see it now. That's the island.

01:03.380 --> 01:08.660
Farmers come over from the main island
when it's harvest time for the sugarcane,

01:08.660 --> 01:13.550
but right now, it's just the observatory 
staff and our guests staying here.

01:13.550 --> 01:17.700
And your famous black sugar syrup
 is made from this sugarcane, right?

01:17.700 --> 01:19.310
You know your stuff!

01:19.910 --> 01:23.340
Sign me up for three meals a day
of high-quality black sugar syrup!

01:23.340 --> 01:25.230
Only you would be okay with that!

01:25.860 --> 01:28.970
And I'd like to attempt 
hula hooping after eating.

01:28.970 --> 01:31.780
<i>That's</i> what you forgot and went back for?!

01:32.490 --> 01:37.840
"Hula hooping at an observatory" is on
 the list I made during my five-year seclusion.

01:37.840 --> 01:39.950
That nonsensical list again...

01:41.370 --> 01:44.320
We're serving a standing buffet tonight.

01:44.320 --> 01:47.090
I'll ask the chef about 
a black sugar syrup meal for you.

01:47.590 --> 01:49.740
And hula hoop to your heart's content.

01:54.940 --> 01:57.140
Now, here we are.

01:57.140 --> 02:00.960
This is the pride and joy of the island, 
Nandan Observatory.

02:14.210 --> 02:17.530
Ron    Kamonohashi's

02:14.210 --> 02:17.530
<i>Forbidden\h\h\h
</i>Deductions

03:32.020 --> 03:36.700
<b>#07   The Case of the Observatory Murder (Part 1)</b>

03:37.990 --> 03:41.050
On the first floor, we have 
the lobby and cafeteria.

03:42.580 --> 03:44.540
Huh? A pistol?

03:44.800 --> 03:47.750
It's a replica. 
The gun wards off evil spirits.

03:48.180 --> 03:49.280
Wow.

03:49.280 --> 03:51.700
It's meticulously crafted.

03:51.700 --> 03:55.590
Nearly indistinguishable from the real thing.
 But what's this about evil spirits?

03:55.590 --> 04:00.110
Long ago on this island,
 in order to protect the sugarcane,

04:00.110 --> 04:03.420
every household kept a flintlock as a charm.

04:03.420 --> 04:04.560
That's the tradition.

04:05.020 --> 04:06.230
Huh!

04:06.940 --> 04:09.830
The second floor holds guestrooms.

04:09.830 --> 04:11.900
And the doors at the end of the hall...

04:11.900 --> 04:14.360
are the entrance to the observation dome.

04:15.820 --> 04:18.370
I'll kill 'em!

04:22.150 --> 04:23.200
Oh, Director.

04:23.200 --> 04:25.240
What are you doing, Unno-kun?

04:25.240 --> 04:26.950
Relieving stress.

04:27.310 --> 04:29.820
With the dome closed, 
this place is soundproof,

04:29.820 --> 04:32.920
so when something ticks me off, 
I come here to scream.

04:32.920 --> 04:35.200
I-I didn't know that.

04:35.200 --> 04:36.960
Just listen to this!

04:36.960 --> 04:39.540
One of the guests, Donzawa, 
asked me to bring coffee.

04:39.540 --> 04:42.930
And when I did, he yelled because
 the stars on the cup were wrong!

04:42.930 --> 04:45.510
Also, what's this about
 a black sugar syrup meal?

04:46.450 --> 04:47.220
That's for me.

04:47.220 --> 04:49.060
A g-guest?!

04:49.060 --> 04:50.770
Please pardon my rudeness!

04:50.770 --> 04:52.770
Sorry for the impossible ask.

04:52.770 --> 04:54.440
What's all the commotion?

04:55.610 --> 04:57.570
<i>That haircut's really something!</i>

04:57.570 --> 05:02.810
My hair is cut so as not to get in the way
when I look through a telescope.

05:02.810 --> 05:05.780
<i>There's so much I want to say, 
but I beg you, mouth! Be still!</i>

05:06.170 --> 05:08.960
Dear, dear. It seems we have impure guests.

05:08.960 --> 05:10.080
Impure?

05:10.080 --> 05:14.150
Donzawa-san means we have people
who can't appreciate the shower,

05:14.150 --> 05:16.300
who aren't astronomy fans, among us.

05:17.380 --> 05:20.220
Hi! I'm Onodera, a photographer 
of celestial objects.

05:20.740 --> 05:22.680
And it isn't just you two.

05:22.680 --> 05:25.440
This guy doesn't seem like
 an astronomy buff either.

05:28.370 --> 05:29.180
You're...

05:29.880 --> 05:31.140
Sensei...

05:31.510 --> 05:32.850
"Sensei"? You mean...

05:32.850 --> 05:33.600
Yes.

05:34.030 --> 05:38.320
He's the BLUE detective academy's
 closed circle theory instructor,

05:38.810 --> 05:40.780
John Grizzly.

05:41.270 --> 05:42.660
He's from BLUE?

05:42.660 --> 05:46.660
He's one of the few instructors 
I acknowledged as my superior.

05:47.060 --> 05:51.120
And why might you be here, 
Kamonohashi... kun?

05:51.500 --> 05:53.170
I'm on a gourmet journey.

05:53.490 --> 05:55.500
Well, you're all here now!

05:55.930 --> 05:59.210
Let me make the introductions. 
This is Grizzly-san and Isshiki-san.

05:59.210 --> 06:03.220
I've asked these two here 
to make sure there's no trouble.

06:03.220 --> 06:06.310
One's a first-class sleuth and the other's 
a renowned police detective.

06:06.310 --> 06:09.050
A man of his caliber playing security?

06:09.050 --> 06:10.680
It's the least they can do...

06:11.220 --> 06:14.900
after the gut-wrenching 
incident that happened here.

06:14.900 --> 06:17.610
Please don't talk about 
incidents in front of me.

06:17.610 --> 06:19.030
I'm not interested at all!

06:19.030 --> 06:21.070
Your words and actions don't add up!

06:21.620 --> 06:24.820
If Toto insists so strongly on hearing 
about it, I guess I don't mind.

06:24.820 --> 06:27.880
You hallucinated me insisting that, 
but let's hear it.

06:30.990 --> 06:33.230
Back then, just like right now,

06:33.230 --> 06:36.960
the conditions for watching the 
Leonid meteor shower were perfect.

06:37.900 --> 06:39.840
It happened ten years ago.

06:39.840 --> 06:41.590
Here at Nandan Observatory,

06:41.630 --> 06:47.180
<b>At the Observatory: 7 People Die Tragically by Gunfire</b>

06:42.180 --> 06:47.180
the director at the time 
and six others were gunned down.

06:50.420 --> 06:54.130
The director then was my father.

06:54.130 --> 06:54.850
What?

06:55.110 --> 06:59.440
Even after a large-scale investigation,
 the gun used was never found.

06:59.440 --> 07:03.190
The killer remains unidentified. 
The case has gone cold.

07:03.190 --> 07:05.990
We considered shutting down the observatory,

07:05.990 --> 07:10.410
but my father loved this place 
and astronomy with all his heart.

07:10.910 --> 07:14.930
Which is why I'm holding a viewing party 
for the same meteor shower.

07:14.930 --> 07:19.130
I think overcoming that tragedy 
is what my father would want!

07:19.450 --> 07:21.350
I wholeheartedly agree, Director!

07:21.350 --> 07:22.840
We're cheering you on!

07:22.840 --> 07:24.750
That's right, Jumonji-san!

07:24.750 --> 07:26.550
Let's make this viewing a success!

07:26.860 --> 07:29.510
Sniffle! That story's enough 
to make a person cry, star.

07:29.510 --> 07:31.970
Huh? Is that...

07:32.490 --> 07:35.660
I couldn't find the right timing to step in.

07:35.660 --> 07:37.850
I was invited here as well.

07:38.600 --> 07:41.180
I'm the idol of the constellation Orion...

07:41.180 --> 07:42.650
Orihime, star!

07:42.950 --> 07:45.730
This is the first time I've met 
an idol in the flesh.

07:45.730 --> 07:48.360
Despite appearances,
she's a pure astronomy fan.

07:52.030 --> 07:53.740
Who's opening that without permission?

07:53.740 --> 07:56.710
Sorry. I couldn't resist pulling the lever.

07:56.710 --> 07:59.480
Oh! The observatory dome is splitting!

08:04.090 --> 08:06.340
The telescope spins?!

08:06.340 --> 08:07.770
It's computer controlled.

08:07.770 --> 08:11.050
It automatically tracks the position 
and records footage of any stars entered.

08:14.020 --> 08:17.860
But we won't be using this telescope 
to watch the meteor shower.

08:18.480 --> 08:21.930
Using a telescope with low magnification,

08:21.930 --> 08:24.460
or just your eyes, 
really captures the beauty of the shower.

08:24.460 --> 08:25.440
Really?

08:25.440 --> 08:28.530
We'll be able to observe it 
starting around 11 PM on the roof.

08:28.530 --> 08:31.990
Until then, please enjoy the standing buffet.

08:43.280 --> 08:44.890
You're fully seated!

08:44.890 --> 08:46.800
And you put that syrup on everything!

08:47.100 --> 08:49.540
Well, what's the harm?

08:49.540 --> 08:54.540
He's charmed us all. 
He's a pure astronomy maniac.

08:54.540 --> 08:55.260
What?

08:55.260 --> 08:59.100
There aren't many people who can 
talk at length so happily

08:59.100 --> 09:00.610
about brown dwarfs.

09:01.150 --> 09:03.360
Ron, I didn't know you were into this.

09:03.820 --> 09:05.650
An ancestor of mine five generations ago

09:05.650 --> 09:08.620
was a detective who didn't know 
about heliocentrism or solar systems.

09:08.620 --> 09:11.320
I developed an interest in reaction to that.

09:11.320 --> 09:13.030
Really?

09:13.700 --> 09:16.740
<i>Now that I think about it, 
I don't know much about Ron.</i>

09:22.940 --> 09:27.140
<i>That man... I wonder if he knows about 
Ron from his time at the academy.</i>

09:27.610 --> 09:29.300
<i>And about his illness, too.</i>

09:29.780 --> 09:33.410
<i>He might even have a hint 
about how to cure it!</i>

09:36.350 --> 09:38.310
G-Good evening.

09:39.200 --> 09:41.940
You are a friend of Kamonohashi-kun, I gather?

09:41.940 --> 09:42.860
Yes.

09:42.860 --> 09:47.020
He isn't participating in any 
forbidden sleuthing, is he?

09:47.020 --> 09:48.380
What? No, sir.

09:49.150 --> 09:52.200
After all, he ends up 
pressuring the perpetrators.

09:52.200 --> 09:55.410
I see. So you know that much about him.

09:55.410 --> 09:57.940
B-But I don't know any of the details!

09:59.790 --> 10:02.230
If you wouldn't mind, 
I was hoping you'd tell me.

10:02.230 --> 10:04.010
What happened in his past?

10:04.010 --> 10:07.380
Did Ron really pressure culprits
to their own deaths?

10:11.560 --> 10:16.810
Five years ago, Ron took part 
in a hands-on training exercise.

10:16.810 --> 10:19.060
Students and police worked together

10:19.060 --> 10:22.020
to the end of catching real culprits.

10:22.020 --> 10:24.270
With his genius deductions,

10:24.270 --> 10:28.940
he succeeded in locating 
the base of a group of seven killers.

10:28.940 --> 10:32.400
But when police entered the stronghold...

10:37.370 --> 10:39.030
Murder weapon in hand,

10:39.030 --> 10:43.470
Kamonohashi Ron was standing there,
 dazed and covered in blood,

10:43.470 --> 10:46.610
among the corpses of all seven murderers.

10:47.420 --> 10:50.420
It became known as the 
Bloody Training Incident.

10:51.110 --> 10:54.030
I believe that's the answer 
you were looking for.

10:54.380 --> 10:56.910
Ron did that to the culprits...?

10:57.340 --> 10:59.970
There is 99 percent certainty.

11:00.710 --> 11:02.850
However, Kamonohashi Ron had no memory

11:02.850 --> 11:05.420
of the thirty minutes before or after,

11:05.420 --> 11:07.940
so he was considered to be
of unsound mind at the time.

11:07.940 --> 11:10.860
As such, barring him from
 a detective's license

11:10.860 --> 11:13.440
was the extent of his punishment.

11:15.160 --> 11:16.910
He's lucky.

11:17.360 --> 11:20.910
Had I been in charge of deciding his fate,

11:20.910 --> 11:22.870
I would have given him the death penalty.

11:27.760 --> 11:30.540
You're Kamonohashi-san's 
friend, aren't you?

11:30.540 --> 11:32.160
Please stop him!

11:32.160 --> 11:32.930
What?

11:36.840 --> 11:39.160
It's dangerous to do that 
after you've just eaten that much!

11:39.160 --> 11:41.990
I was depicting the orbit 
of planets in a solar system...

11:41.990 --> 11:43.310
It was magnificent!

11:43.310 --> 11:44.270
Yes, it was!

11:45.540 --> 11:47.590
I am utterly content, Toto.

11:48.780 --> 11:52.540
Since I've achieved my goal and I'm sleepy, 
I'm going to my room.

11:52.540 --> 11:53.820
And the meteor shower?

11:54.570 --> 11:56.070
I'll see it in my dreams.

11:56.700 --> 11:57.680
That's so deep.

11:57.680 --> 11:58.860
How refined.

11:58.860 --> 12:00.620
You've made some die-hard fans!

12:02.080 --> 12:05.540
<i>That Ron! He has no idea 
how I feel right now...</i>

12:15.820 --> 12:16.880
So this...

12:17.620 --> 12:19.810
is the Leonid meteor shower!

12:21.690 --> 12:26.600
<i>I have absolutely no interest in the stars, 
but I'm so glad I came.</i>

12:33.810 --> 12:36.660
Come to think of it, 
where did Onodera-san go?

12:36.660 --> 12:38.910
She hurried back to her room.

12:38.910 --> 12:41.320
Said something about getting
 photography equipment.

12:41.860 --> 12:44.030
But it's been about two hours, hasn't it?

12:48.710 --> 12:49.990
The dome!

12:53.770 --> 12:55.040
Was that a gunshot?!

12:55.040 --> 12:55.840
It was inside!

12:55.840 --> 12:56.800
It can't be...

12:56.800 --> 12:57.790
I'll go and see!

12:57.790 --> 12:58.760
Yes!

13:03.760 --> 13:04.640
It's no use.

13:04.640 --> 13:06.430
I'll go get the key!

13:08.810 --> 13:10.190
What's happened, star?

13:12.230 --> 13:14.190
Is anyone in there?!

13:19.490 --> 13:20.900
I can't find the key!

13:20.900 --> 13:22.530
It should be in the office, but...

13:22.530 --> 13:23.220
What?!

13:23.220 --> 13:23.870
But that's...

13:23.870 --> 13:25.880
All we can do is break down the door.

13:29.440 --> 13:30.960
It's certainly sturdy.

13:30.960 --> 13:32.210
I'll help too!

13:32.210 --> 13:33.410
So will I!

13:39.120 --> 13:40.340
It's pitch black.

13:44.360 --> 13:45.640
The lights won't turn on.

13:45.640 --> 13:48.030
Director! I got flashlights!

13:48.030 --> 13:49.910
That's a huge help, Unno-kun!

13:54.120 --> 13:55.640
I-It can't be.

13:55.640 --> 13:58.150
That's Onodera-san and...

14:00.550 --> 14:01.730
Ron?!

14:03.420 --> 14:05.320
Th-This can't be happening.

14:08.610 --> 14:09.330
Ron!

14:22.090 --> 14:24.300
Sh-She's dead!

14:24.750 --> 14:29.310
I've been such a fool.
I should have predicted this.

14:29.310 --> 14:32.020
Y-You don't suspect Ron, do you?

14:32.020 --> 14:34.180
Just look! It's obvious, isn't it?!

14:35.900 --> 14:38.390
I thought he was suspicious from the start!

14:38.390 --> 14:40.730
What weirdo wants a black sugar syrup meal?!

14:41.110 --> 14:42.690
The syrup did nothing wrong.

14:43.760 --> 14:44.910
Ron, you're awake?

14:45.550 --> 14:48.480
I woke to Orihime-kun screaming.

14:48.480 --> 14:52.370
I don't remember anything after going 
back to my room and lying down on my bed.

14:52.910 --> 14:58.590
But I can deduce from your conversation 
that I'm in a very bad situation right now.

14:58.590 --> 15:00.260
This was a murder!

15:00.260 --> 15:01.860
Hurry up and restrain him!

15:01.860 --> 15:04.990
Please, no one move! 
All of you are suspects too.

15:04.990 --> 15:05.590
What?

15:06.960 --> 15:08.390
W-We are?

15:08.390 --> 15:14.190
I make it a point to look at every incident 
fairly and without prejudice.

15:14.510 --> 15:18.420
I must treat everyone here 
on the island as a suspect.

15:19.450 --> 15:23.800
You are truly an instructor 
who embodies BLUE's lofty ideals.

15:23.800 --> 15:26.690
Therein lies the reason I doff my cap to you.

15:27.040 --> 15:30.640
Please, investigate this thoroughly, 
first-rate sleuth...

15:30.640 --> 15:32.040
and renowned police detective.

15:32.940 --> 15:35.080
<i>Right. I have to do this too.</i>

15:35.790 --> 15:38.330
I haven't eliminated you as a suspect.

15:38.330 --> 15:41.060
Stay quiet and watch, Kamonohashi Ron.

15:43.420 --> 15:47.260
The body is still warm, meaning she's 
only very recently deceased.

15:47.730 --> 15:51.130
The bullet struck her heart 
directly through her back.

15:51.130 --> 15:54.120
Strictly speaking, we need to
 wait for an autopsy first,

15:54.120 --> 15:55.480
but this is most likely the cause of death.

15:56.620 --> 15:58.740
So the murder weapon was a gun.

15:58.740 --> 16:00.270
I'll hold on to this.

16:00.270 --> 16:03.380
That gun was on display in the lobby!

16:03.380 --> 16:05.690
I never imagined that it was real...

16:10.050 --> 16:12.570
All of the lights in here are broken.

16:16.400 --> 16:20.500
With no ladder, escape through 
the dome would be impossible.

16:22.780 --> 16:25.660
No one's escaping through here either.

16:25.660 --> 16:27.420
Yeah, it's way too small.

16:32.520 --> 16:35.310
There don't seem to be exits anywhere else.

16:35.310 --> 16:37.020
I-I agree.

16:37.630 --> 16:41.750
Therefore, we can only say that
 these mounting facts lead us

16:41.750 --> 16:43.430
to but a single truth.

16:44.100 --> 16:48.190
It's impossible to think the culprit was
 anyone except you, Kamonohashi Ron.

16:48.190 --> 16:49.650
See?! I knew it!

16:49.650 --> 16:52.990
Oh? That's not the result I was hoping for.

16:52.990 --> 16:54.310
B-But...

16:54.310 --> 16:57.330
There's undeniable circumstantial
 evidence against you.

16:57.800 --> 16:59.710
The same as five years ago.

17:02.200 --> 17:05.380
There is no way in or out other than 
the door we came through.

17:05.820 --> 17:08.340
But that door was locked.

17:08.800 --> 17:11.440
So inside this observation dome...

17:11.440 --> 17:14.050
was a perfect locked room.

17:14.050 --> 17:15.010
What?

17:15.470 --> 17:16.720
A locked room?

17:17.240 --> 17:20.460
Just because the door 
was locked, I'm the culprit?

17:20.460 --> 17:22.040
I killed some—

17:23.000 --> 17:24.050
Clink?

17:27.570 --> 17:30.190
What is this?

17:30.530 --> 17:34.420
That's the key from the lobby! 
It's the only master key!

17:34.420 --> 17:38.830
Wh-What's this troublesome thing
doing in my pocket?

17:38.830 --> 17:40.760
That's definitive proof!

17:40.760 --> 17:41.830
Murderer!

17:41.830 --> 17:43.540
What? Why would Ron kill someone?

17:43.540 --> 17:46.000
Arrest him, Isshiki-kun.

17:48.420 --> 17:49.680
Please wait!

17:49.680 --> 17:53.430
It's all right, Toto. If you're the one 
arresting me, then I'm satisfied.

17:53.430 --> 17:56.510
Wh-What? Ron! 
Don't you have anything to say?

17:56.510 --> 17:59.970
No. I've got nothing.

18:00.260 --> 18:01.560
No way...

18:01.560 --> 18:04.810
Go and bring him his shoes, Isshiki-kun.

18:07.200 --> 18:10.490
It's dangerous to walk over 
these shards barefoot.

18:16.010 --> 18:16.940
Yes, sir.

18:18.740 --> 18:21.070
This observatory is cursed!

18:21.070 --> 18:23.080
Please don't say such scary things!

18:23.080 --> 18:25.830
She's right!
 We've caught the culprit, after all.

18:25.830 --> 18:30.050
Jumonji-san, please contact 
the police on the main island.

18:30.050 --> 18:32.220
We still require a formal investigation.

18:32.220 --> 18:35.890
I will. Having you here 
really saved us, Grizzly-san.

18:38.440 --> 18:40.740
You really don't remember anything?

18:41.250 --> 18:45.460
No. My memory stops
 at collapsing onto my bed.

18:45.460 --> 18:48.350
When I opened my eyes, 
I was in the observatory dome.

18:48.350 --> 18:51.940
Along with the body of Onodera-kun, 
whom I seem to have killed.

18:52.630 --> 18:53.990
Is that...

18:54.520 --> 18:57.130
how you felt after the
 Bloody Training Incident?

18:58.640 --> 19:01.220
Did Grizzly-sensei tell you about that?

19:01.220 --> 19:03.070
During dinner.

19:03.700 --> 19:06.580
It's exactly the same, right down 
to the crime I committed.

19:07.000 --> 19:09.710
You seriously think you're the killer?

19:09.710 --> 19:14.010
I must be. I can't remember anything,
 so it must be true.

19:14.010 --> 19:15.620
Hold it, Ron!

19:15.620 --> 19:17.780
What's going on? This isn't like you!

19:17.780 --> 19:20.010
Did your brain get rusty or something?

19:20.010 --> 19:22.400
You're talking like you have
 proof to the contrary.

19:22.400 --> 19:23.350
I do!

19:23.350 --> 19:24.700
Just think about it!

19:24.700 --> 19:27.270
The victim was just a regular person.

19:27.270 --> 19:31.860
The only people you've tried to pressure 
to death have always been murderers, right?

19:33.500 --> 19:37.410
You've never once tried 
to kill an innocent person.

19:37.410 --> 19:40.370
You said you weren't that kind of man.

19:40.370 --> 19:42.870
You lose heart instantly
 when it comes to this,

19:42.870 --> 19:44.080
so I'll say it again!

19:45.290 --> 19:48.000
Even if you aren't sure, I am!

19:50.550 --> 19:56.040
Your declaration seems to have warmed up 
my frozen brain just a little.

19:56.040 --> 19:58.510
That's right... I just remembered something.

19:58.510 --> 20:01.350
There <i>is</i> one point I found strange.

20:01.350 --> 20:02.050
What?

20:02.390 --> 20:06.350
In truth, I've kept a secret from you.

20:06.350 --> 20:08.060
A-A secret?

20:08.830 --> 20:10.770
You see, Toto, I...

20:13.790 --> 20:16.400
I am completely useless with a gun.

20:16.400 --> 20:17.860
Wha?!

20:18.220 --> 20:21.520
I always earned perfect scores
 in every other subject.

20:21.520 --> 20:23.010
But not marksmanship.

20:23.010 --> 20:26.390
I failed for never being able 
to so much as graze a target.

20:26.390 --> 20:27.710
For real?

20:28.710 --> 20:32.670
But Onodera-san was shot 
precisely in the heart from behind.

20:32.670 --> 20:37.130
Even if I had a thousand bullets,
with my skills, I wouldn't land a single shot.

20:37.130 --> 20:39.400
Then there's no way you killed her.

20:39.400 --> 20:43.050
Wait, why didn't you say so earlier?
That's super important!

20:43.050 --> 20:45.910
Because in the five years since 
the Bloody Training Incident,

20:45.910 --> 20:48.520
I've kept telling myself...

20:48.880 --> 20:51.640
if I ever slipped up and couldn't remember it,

20:51.640 --> 20:54.990
then as hard as it might be to accept,
I'd give up without a fight.

20:54.990 --> 20:55.920
What?

20:55.920 --> 20:59.320
I had to tell myself that to stay sane.

20:59.320 --> 21:02.840
I resented the victims, BLUE, the world...

21:02.840 --> 21:05.450
I was nearly a criminal.

21:06.030 --> 21:07.660
You mean...

21:07.660 --> 21:09.600
<i>In his heart, Ron doesn't really think</i>

21:09.600 --> 21:13.110
<i>he was the culprit in the
Bloody Training Incident.</i>

21:13.750 --> 21:15.030
Thank you.

21:15.030 --> 21:17.940
Toto, thanks to you, the ice 
freezing up my thoughts has melted.

21:17.940 --> 21:20.890
My brain's now working at about one percent.

21:20.890 --> 21:22.590
A single percent, huh?

21:23.100 --> 21:28.390
Hey, if I'm not the culprit, does that 
mean you think someone else did it?

21:28.390 --> 21:29.810
Well, of course.

21:30.370 --> 21:32.270
Hang on. That means...

21:32.670 --> 21:34.730
If the culprit's still out there...

21:35.790 --> 21:40.950
<i>That means one of them killed Onodera-san 
and framed Ron as the murderer.</i>

21:41.780 --> 21:43.120
I've gotta go!

21:43.120 --> 21:43.660
Where?

21:43.660 --> 21:45.330
To investigate, of course!

21:54.720 --> 21:58.590
I cried and screamed when I was arrested
five years ago, didn't I?

21:59.350 --> 22:03.050
I've finally figured out why 
I'm not as panicked this time.

22:05.890 --> 22:09.060
Five years ago, I didn't have Toto.
